  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Part of the Hippodrome beach, in Cagnes-sur-Mer, is reserved for dogs — with the nice bonus of a shower to rinse off the salt and sand after swimming. It's the only option in the town for dog owners.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Precise location confirmed by two matching sources (including the official Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office): the area lies between groyne 1 and groyne 2, at the boundary with Villeneuve-Loubet. On the leash rule, there's a contradiction: we used to state it as mandatory, but these same tourism sources instead describe a tolerance without a leash as long as the dog stays under control, outside the summer season (June to October) — without confirmation from an official municipal source, a leash remains the safest choice.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this is a good stop between Nice and Villeneuve-Loubet if you're combining several dog-friendly spots in one day.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Plage de Vaugrenier in Villeneuve-Loubet, also fitted with a dog shower, is a few minutes away by car.</p>
    </div>

